{
  "format": "pala-1 inference profile payload digest vectors",
  "profile_section": "docs/specs/pala-1/profiles/inference.md, section 11",
  "purpose": "EVT_PAYLOAD_DIGEST and ORIGIN_CONFIG_DIGEST are SHA-256 over RFC 8785 canonical JSON, UTF-8. These cases let another implementation check that it computes the same digest - and none where the profile says a value has no canonical form.",
  "how_to_read": [
    "json_text is the value as JSON text. Read it with a parser that keeps a repeated key in sight and reads an integer exactly: both are lost by a parser that returns a map and a double.",
    "A case with sha256 is digested: canonical_utf8_hex is the canonical form and sha256 its digest.",
    "A case with digest null has no canonical form. The emitter records the event without EVT_PAYLOAD_DIGEST; it does not substitute a form of its own.",
    "A deep case gives a recipe instead of text: 'array' at depth n is n arrays, each holding the next, the innermost empty; 'object' at depth n is n objects, each holding the next under the key k, the innermost holding 0."
  ],
  "reasons": {
    "integer_out_of_range": "an integer beyond +-(2^53 - 1), written without a fraction or an exponent (RFC 7493 section 2.2)",
    "repeated_key": "an object gives a key more than once (RFC 7493 section 2.3)",
    "not_unicode": "a string holds an unpaired surrogate (RFC 8785 section 3.2.2.2)",
    "not_finite": "NaN or an infinity (RFC 8785 section 3.2.2.3)",
    "nested_too_deep": "more than 128 arrays and objects, one inside another"
  },
  "reasons_note": "The reason is for the reader of this file. An emitter does not record it: the event carries no digest, and that is all the chain says.",
  "counts": {
    "digested": 22,
    "no_digest": 15
  },
